@Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5276

# Requests for the mock wallet, against the frozen seed (data/seed/README.md). The contract is docs/wallet-api.md.
# User 1 (07805550001) is the demo user and users 1 to 5 exist; 07805550101 is Hammoudi (contact S01 of user 1, not a user);
# bill account 1 is user 1's home electricity; product 1 is Zain credit 5,000.
# Change @idempotencyKey before each new payment: a used key replays the stored outcome instead of paying again.
# Keys are 1 to 64 characters of A-Z, a-z, 0-9, _ and -, not starting with seed-; anything else is 400 invalid_idempotency_key.
# A used key sent with a different body (user, type, amount, recipient, bill or product) is 422 idempotency_key_reused.
@idempotencyKey = http-demo-001

# Every request except /health carries the X-Wallet-Client-Key header. In Development with no Wallet:ClientKey set, any
# non-empty value is accepted (the header is there so a browser must preflight). With a key set, put the key here instead.
@clientKey = tests

# Every /admin request also carries the X-Wallet-Admin-Key header. In Development with no Wallet:AdminKey set, any non-empty
# value is accepted (the header is there so a browser must preflight). With a key set, put the key here instead.
@adminKey = dev

### Health
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/health

### One user
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### User 5 gives consent (204; again is also 204; a reset clears it, as it clears everyone's)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/5/consent
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### The wallet account behind a phone number (registered name and status, active or closed)
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/accounts/by-phone/07805550101
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Contacts and aliases of user 1 (add ?q= to filter by a substring of the saved name or alias)
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/contacts
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Save an alias of user 1 for one account (milestone 9a; 201, then 409 alias_exists with the same text; a reset removes it)
# targetAccountId is a targetAccountId from the contacts above; the text is stored trimmed, 1 to 100 characters
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/aliases
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "sample alias",
  "targetAccountId": 6
}

### Delete one alias of user 1 (put an aliasId from the contacts above; 204, then 404 unknown_alias again or for another user's alias)
DELETE {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/aliases/1
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Bills of user 1
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/bills
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Balance of user 1
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/balance
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### History of user 1: transfers to Hammoudi, newest first
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/history?to=07805550101&take=10
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Store catalogue: Zain credit cards
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/store/products?provider=Zain&type=credit
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### The wallet's fees and PIN limits (read only)
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/settings
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Orders of user 1
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/users/1/orders
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Quote: 50,000 to Hammoudi (no money moves)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/quotes
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "transfer",
  "amountIqd": 50000,
  "toPhone": "07805550101"
}

### Quote: pay bill account 1 in full
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/quotes
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "bill",
  "billAccountId": 1
}

### Execute: 50,000 to Hammoudi (201 the first time, 200 replay with the same key)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "transfer",
  "amountIqd": 50000,
  "toPhone": "07805550101"
}

### Execute: pay bill account 1 (amount comes from the wallet)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}-bill

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "bill",
  "billAccountId": 1
}

### Execute: buy product 1 (the response carries the purchase code)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}-purchase

{
  "userId": 1,
  "type": "purchase",
  "productId": 1
}

### Look up the transfer by its key (userId is required; another user gets 404)
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/transactions/by-key/{{idempotencyKey}}?userId=1
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}

### Current fault switch
GET {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Fault: the next execute waits 300 ms, then runs normally
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "mode": "slow",
  "delayMs": 300,
  "once": true
}

### Fault: the next execute commits, then hangs for the configured delay (look it up by key meanwhile)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "mode": "timeoutAfterExecute",
  "once": true
}

### Clear the fault switch
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/faults
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "mode": "none"
}

### External debit: take 5,000 IQD from U1 from outside the agent (milestone 8)
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/debit
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "userId": 1,
  "amountIqd": 5000
}

### Reset: restore the seed, every user not consented, and clear faults
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/reset
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### Reset keeping the seed's consent values (U1 to U4 consented, U5 not), as the runner and the tests do; any other consent value is 422 invalid_consent
POST {{Wallet.MockApi_HostAddress}}/admin/reset?consent=seed
X-Wallet-Client-Key: {{clientKey}}
X-Wallet-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
